[Music]  welcome back to cbs mornings a married  couple is suing a fertility clinic and  its owner over an ivf mix-up that led  two women to give birth to the other  person's baby  daphna and alexander cardinale accuse  the clinic of breach of contract and  medical malpractice now they say the  clinic and its owner handed their embryo  to a third party lab without their  knowledge this lawsuit alleges that the  lab had a history of mishandling the  embryos maria virial spoke to the couple  who say the mistake has left them with  lasting damage  it wasn't so easy naturally for us for  the second one  after having their first child daphna  and alexander cardinale needed help  having a second  using in vitro fertilization they got  pregnant and welcomed a baby girl in  september 2019  but immediately alexander felt something  was wrong  when was the point where you said  something's not right i had a weird sort  of a gut  reaction when she was born it was  anything logical it was just  it was just like a  instinct like a god like something  didn't feel right the baby didn't  resemble either parent and appear to be  of a different race  after two months of growing doubts they  ordered a dna test what was it like  opening those results  the whole thing feels so yeah  terrifying just numb  the tests confirmed their worst fear the  infant was not their biological daughter  when i found out she wasn't mine  and so i had like poured mo i poured  more love into her  i was just so scared i was going to lose  her which i ultimately did  daphna was implanted with a stranger's  embryo who in turn received theirs that  woman who wishes to remain anonymous  gave birth a week later to the  cardinali's biological daughter the  babies were four months old when this  was all figured out and the process of  returning the children to their  biological parents began  the cardinalis had to break the news to  their older daughter olivia having to  tell her that her four-month-old baby  sister  wasn't really her sister and that  there was another baby that  it was just a whole how do you say that  to a five-year-old and we struggled with  that for so long  we finally told her and  you know i think it's really profoundly  changed her the cardinality family is  now suing their physician the california  center for reproductive health and a  third party embryology lab for alleged  misconduct including medical malpractice  and negligence  according to the complaint ccrh thought  that the embryos had gotten mixed up  when an embryology lab in vitro tech was  taking biopsies to send in for genetic  testing in january of 2020 the  cardinalis brought home their biological  daughter zoe for good a bittersweet  moment that also brought a sense of  guilt and loss over the baby they gave  away when we  brought zoe home and we didn't know her  so we had to learn her and learn and  then track all that stuff like i i  watched her have to switch slowly from  caring and tracking from one baby to  another almost like morning  a child even though she wasn't the  couple says they're now fighting for  accountability someone needs to take  responsibility for this mistake  the cardinals say they keep in touch  with the other family and visit them a  couple times a month including birthdays  and holidays we did reach out to the  physician the clinic and the lab named  in this lawsuit but have yet to hear  back from any of them nate  maria thank you so much that is an  unbelievable story gosh i feel so angry  and so sad at the same time listen baby  luca kirby favorite daughter kirby son  also known as my grandson's only seven  weeks old and i see how much you bond so  quickly plus imagine the baby you gave  birth to wasn't yours so all that all  the kicking wasn't your baby  and now you have to deal with that but  i'm glad that it hap if it has to happen  that it's four months the baby won't  remember it's early enough it's early  enough but the parents will never forget  and you're never going to get those  three months back no you're not with  your baby that father thinking to  himself something's not right but maybe  i'm just you know thinking things you  know it's it's a it's a hard time in  your life in general you're not sleeping  and then to get that answer imagine  opening that envelope right wow he puts  in perspective it's like mourning the  loss of one and then learning an  entirely new baby that sums it up yeah  great stuff

